/-!
# Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.18

Clause list from the source:
(a) `G` is a finite group.
(b) `A1`, `A2`, `A3` are subsets of `G` (quantifier domain: `Set G`).
(c) The multiplication map `A1 × A2 × A3 → G`,
  `(a1, a2, a3) ↦ a1 * a2 * a3`, is bijective.
(d) `⟨A2⟩` denotes the subgroup of `G` generated by `A2`.
(e) Question: for all such data, does `|A2|` divide the order of `⟨A2⟩`?
-/

/-- Exact three-factor factorization of a group: the multiplication map
on the subtypes is bijective ([KOU-21.18] Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.18 hypothesis). -/
def IsExactThreeFactorization {G : Type*} [Group G] (A1 A2 A3 : Set G) : Prop :=
  Function.Bijective (fun p : ↥A1 × (↥A2 × ↥A3) => (↑p.1 * ↑p.2.1 * ↑p.2.2 : G))

/-- Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.18 question ([KOU-21.18]): for every finite
group `G` and every exact three-factor factorization `A1, A2, A3`, does
`|A2|` divide the order of `⟨A2⟩`? -/
def conjecture : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type*) [Group G] [Finite G] (A1 A2 A3 : Set G),
    IsExactThreeFactorization A1 A2 A3 → Set.ncard A2 ∣ Nat.card ↥(Subgroup.closure A2)

/--
Resolved false: Answered negatively: M. I. Kabenyuk, Factorizations of finite groups
(arXiv:2102.08605), Proposition 2.3, gives an exact factorization A₄ = A·B·C with |B| = 2 and
|⟨B⟩| = 3. The Kourovka Notebook (arXiv:1401.0300v49) marks Problem 21.18 solved with this
reference. Source: M. I. Kabenyuk, Factorizations of finite groups, arXiv:2102.08605 (2021),
https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.08605; E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (20 October 2026), Problem
21.18, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49. Moved from
`OpenConjectures/Algebra/KourovkaExactFactorizationDivisibility`.
-/
public theorem_wanted conjecture_refuted : ¬ conjecture

end MathlibExt.Algebra.KourovkaExactFactorizationDivisibilityWanted
